# No matching signatures renders `.Length` as `uint()`

Found 2026-09-01 via `./build.sh` on `tm-control-mcp`. Two errors, one spelling.

## Live errors

```
src/DevMemoryTools.as:282:50: error: No matching signatures to 'Math::Min(uint, uint())'
src/DevMemoryTools.as:295:53: error: No matching signatures to 'Math::Min(uint, uint())'
```

Call sites (DEV tool `DevGetPointers`):

```angelscript
auto anchored = editor.Challenge.AnchoredObjects; // MwFastBuffer<CGameCtnAnchoredObject*>
uint take = Math::Min(uint(aoLimit), anchored.Length);

auto blocks = editor.Challenge.Blocks;
uint take = Math::Min(uint(blockLimit), blocks.Length);
```

`uint(aoLimit)` renders as `uint`. `anchored.Length` renders as `uint()`.

That `uint()` is the defect. It is B108's zero-arg function-signature spelling (`return_type(params)`), not a uint value. `.Length` is a uint property/field on the buffer. The game treats it as a uint everywhere else in this plugin (`int(map.Blocks.Length)`, `for (uint i = 0; i < map.Blocks.Length; i++)`, `uint total = pmt.Items.Length`).

## Discriminator in the same function

Ten lines later, the Length is assigned to a uint local first:

```angelscript
uint total = pmt.Items.Length;
uint take = Math::Min(uint(pmtItemsLimit), total); // silent
```

Same `Math::Min`, same `uint(...)` first arg. Only the direct `.Length` argument prints as `uint()`. The local does not.

Also silent in this plugin: `Math::Min(limit, pmt.CustomSelectionCoords.Length)` (`src/McpTools.as:728`) and `Math::Min(len, 8)` on a uint local (`src/DevMemoryTools.as:582`). So this is not "Math::Min has no uint overload" as a general fact — the checker already accepts some uint Mins. Do not "fix" this by adding a uint `Math::Min`. The second argument is being named as a function.

## Why this spelling

`rendered_args` / `funcdef_binding_source_display` (B108): when `lookup_arg_function_sigs` finds exactly one signature, the argument prints as `return_type(params)`. A `uint Length()` / `uint get_Length()` method on the buffer becomes `uint()`.

B060 already said a property READ is a value of the getter's return type, not a reference to the accessor, and made `lookup_arg_function_sigs` exact (no `X` → `get_X` widening). Member path still goes through `method_ref_sigs(object, member)`, which looks up a method named `Length` on the receiver. If the typedb (or template instantiation) exposes `Length` as a method, B108 will print `uint()` and the call looks like a missing `Math::Min` overload.

## Expected

A `.Length` read used as a value renders as `uint` (same as `uint(aoLimit)` and as the `uint total = ….Length` local). If `Math::Min(uint, uint)` then still fails, that is a different question and not this ticket.

## Actual

`.Length` renders as `uint()` — a function returning uint and taking no arguments.

## Test plan (TDD, red first)

Red: the two live lines, or a one-file plugin:

```angelscript
void Use(CGameCtnChallenge@ map) {
    Math::Min(uint(20), map.AnchoredObjects.Length);
    Math::Min(uint(20), map.Blocks.Length);
}
```

The diagnostic text must not contain `uint()`. Variants:

- `MwFastBuffer` `.Length` passed to any non-funcdef call (`Math::Min`, `tostring`, `Text::Format`)
- assign to `uint` first, then pass the local — stays silent / still not `uint()`
- `array<T>.Length` (script array) as a control
- an actual method reference of type `uint()` still prints `uint()` (keep B108)
- `uint get_Off(); Math::Min(uint(1), Off)` — B060 value, not `uint()`

Game-probe the fixture before treating LSP silence as ground truth.

## Related

B060 (property read is a value), B108 (callables print their signature, which is why this shows up as `uint()` instead of `uint`), GH #47 (No matching signatures render). Live plugin: `~/src/openplanet/my-plugins/tm-control-mcp` `src/DevMemoryTools.as:282,295`.